Third-party software
--------------------
The Designer binary bundles third-party software, each under its own licence.
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md lists every package with its licence text. In particular:

- Excalidraw (MIT) provides the canvas. It bundles these fonts, under their
  own licences as published upstream (https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw):
  Virgil, Excalifont, Cascadia, Comic Shanns, Liberation, Lilita One, Nunito,
  Xiaolai and Assistant.
- Inter and JetBrains Mono (SIL Open Font License 1.1) are the UI fonts.
- Tabler Icons (MIT, https://tabler.io/icons) supply the component icons.
- elkjs (used under EPL-2.0, https://github.com/kieler/elkjs) lays out the
  Production Diagram. It is shipped unmodified; its source is available at
  that address.

Document structures
-------------------
Documents Designer generates follow published structures, credited in each
document, in Designer's own wording:

- arc42 architecture documentation template, by Dr. Peter Hruschka,
  Dr. Gernot Starke and contributors (https://arc42.org), CC BY-SA 4.0.
  Generated arc42 documents use its section headings.
- Threat Modeling Manifesto (https://www.threatmodelingmanifesto.org),
  CC BY 4.0: the four questions structure the Threat model.
- MADR 4.0, Markdown Architectural Decision Records (https://adr.github.io/madr/):
  the layout of exported ADRs.
- ISO/IEC/IEEE 29148 (requirements specification outline), NIST SP 800-34
  (contingency planning) and the STRIDE threat categories are followed for
  structure only; no text is reproduced.

Knowledge Base
--------------
The Knowledge Base (kb/records) is written by the Designer authors and is
covered by this product's licence (see docs/adr/0002). Records cite their
sources; text is copied verbatim only from public-domain sources (the HIPAA
Security Rule, 45 CFR Part 164). SOC 2 Trust Services Criteria are
(c) AICPA and are referenced by identifier only; no AICPA text is reproduced.

The reference copies in kb/sources are not built into the binary and keep
their own licences, listed in kb/sources/README.md (OWASP Cheat Sheet Series,
CC BY-SA 4.0; AWS documentation, CC BY-SA 4.0; Azure Architecture Center,
CC BY 4.0; 45 CFR 164.312, public domain).

Cloud provider names (AWS, Azure) are trademarks of their owners and are used
only to identify the services a diagram targets.
